---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy & cookies"
  description="Learn how this website uses analytics with your consent, saves your cookie choice, and handles privacy requests."
>
  <article class="privacy-notice">
    <h1>Privacy & cookies</h1>
    <p>Last updated: 18 October 2026</p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      I’m Madis Burmeister, based in Estonia, and I’m responsible for this
      website’s analytics. For privacy questions or requests, email
      {" "}<a href="mailto:madis.burmeister@mabux.me">madis.burmeister@mabux.me</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Optional website analytics</h2>
    <p>
      With your permission, this website uses Google Analytics 4 (GA4), a service
      from Google Ireland Limited. It helps me understand how people use the site,
      including which pages they visit, how they engage, and when they download my
      resume or click an email link. An email-link click shows an attempt to
      contact me; it doesn’t mean an enquiry was completed. I don’t use analytics
      for advertising.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google receives technical details such as your device and browser, your
      approximate location based on your IP address, visit times, and cookie
      identifiers. Google says GA4 does not log or store individual IP addresses.
      This website’s page-view events don’t include URL query strings or
      fragments. Email addresses and message contents aren’t included when you
      click an email link.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google Analytics doesn’t load, set cookies, or send requests until you
      choose “Accept analytics.” I use your consent as the legal basis for this
      optional data processing. You can reject analytics and still use the whole
      website.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and saved choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>mabux.analytics-consent.v1:</strong>{" "}saves your choice in this
        device’s local storage for 180 days. It only remembers whether you
        accepted or rejected analytics; it doesn’t track your visits.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>_ga and _ga_*:</strong>{" "}optional first-party Google Analytics
        cookies that identify your browser and keep session information. They’re
        set to expire after 60 days and aren’t extended on each visit. Your
        browser may remove them sooner.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Use <button type="button" data-cookie-settings>Cookies</button> to
      change your choice. If you reject after accepting, the website stops future
      tracking, removes the first-party Analytics cookies it can access, and
      reloads to stop Analytics. This doesn’t undo earlier data processing.
      Clearing your browser storage removes your saved choice.
    </p>

    <h2>Google processing and retention</h2>
    <p>
      Google processes analytics data for me. It may process it outside the
      European Economic Area, including in the United States, under applicable
      contractual and international data-transfer safeguards. Read{" "}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s privacy policy</a>{" "}
      and learn <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses data from sites that use its services</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      GA4 keeps user- and event-level data for two months. It may keep combined
      reports for longer. This data-retention period is separate from the cookie
      lifetime above. This website’s Google tag doesn’t enable Google signals or
      advertising personalization.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting, fonts, embedded content and contacting me</h2>
    <p>
      GitHub Pages hosts this website and may process technical details, such as
      IP addresses, to deliver and protect it. Google Fonts receives your IP
      address and browser request details when fonts load, whether or not you
      accept analytics. Some project pages include third-party embeds that also
      receive technical details when loaded. Rejecting analytics doesn’t block
      fonts or embeds.
    </p>
    <p>
      External websites have their own privacy practices. If you email me, I
      receive the information you choose to send and use it to reply and manage
      our correspondence. I keep correspondence only as long as needed to handle
      your enquiry, maintain our working relationship, or meet legal obligations.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on your situation, you can ask to access, correct, or delete your
      personal data, limit how it’s used, or receive it in a portable format. You
      can also object to processing based on legitimate interests and withdraw
      your analytics consent at any time. Email me using the address above. I may
      ask for details to identify your data. You can also complain to Estonia’s{" "}
      <a href="https://www.aki.ee/en">Data Protection Inspectorate</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy-notice { max-width: 48rem; margin: 0 auto; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); }
  h2 { margin-top: 2rem; font-size: 1.5rem; }
  p, ul { margin-top: 1rem; }
  p { text-align: justify; }
  ul { list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.5rem; }
  li + li { margin-top: 0.75rem; }
  a, button { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 0.2em; }
  button { cursor: pointer; }
</style>
